      "message": "This is a very WIP CL that, per b/361604548, takes the shading uniform cache off of Recorders and makes it local to DrawPass creation, as we do with the render step uniform cache. It\u0027s then able to remove a de-duplication step by using a new cache class that holds the de-duplicated data and returns indices into this data which is then written directly to uniform buffers, rather than having the old UniformTracker\u0027s extra layer of mapping from index to de-duplicated data pointers.\n\nSome particularly WIP stuff includes:\n- We want to merge functionality between UniformDataCache and DenseBiMap instead of adding a new cache class\n- BufferInfo.fStartAlignment is no longer used for storage buffers, instead the requested stride is used to align new writers\n- The BufferManager is essentially overloading BindBufferInfo.fOffset with a storage buffer index, and assuming it will be used as such rather than as a binding offset. This seems like something that could cause confusion down the road\n- ContextUtil\u0027s Extract*Data functions are inlined, for convenience of testing this approach out\n- This also doesn\u0027t *actually* remove the UniformDataCache field from Recorder yet, because that causes a lot of files to recompile when I switch between branches locally\n\nSo far these changes seem to yield better performance in motionmark benchmarks when the storage buffer block size is tweaked (upwards).",
